<title>USA: USDA sets Aug 5 meeting on transgenic plants.</title>
<headline>USDA sets Aug 5 meeting on transgenic plants.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-07-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Agriculture Department said it scheduled an Aug 5 workshop in suburban Washington to discuss the problems of virus-resistant plants used to genetically engineer stronger strains.</p>
<p>Registration for the workshop will be accepted until two weeks prior to the session.</p>
<p>The all-day meeting will be held at the USDA center in Riverdale, Maryland.</p>
<p>The agency's Animal and Plant Health Inspection Service said the workshop would focus on the likelihood of a new virus appearing through genetic engineering and the transmision of virus-resistant genes, among other issues.</p>
<p>((Washington commodities desk 202 898 8467))</p>
